          "instructions": "SMS freeze (send from your registered mobile number): BLOCKUPI <Customer ID> (example BLOCKUPI 123456) — 'Helps you block your UPI access'; BLOCKALL <Customer ID> (example BLOCKALL 123456) — 'Helps you block your Internet Banking, Mobile Banking and UPI access'; send keywords to SMS Banking numbers 56161600 or +91 9951860002. NPCI UPI Help (upihelp.npci.org.in, linked from Axis's UPI page) offers a Safety Switch to 'pause outgoing UPI debit transactions from the selected account' — 'Outgoing UPI debit transactions from the selected account are blocked. Incoming UPI credits continue.'; it cannot be resumed there: 'contact Axis Bank Phone Banking or visit your nearest Axis Bank branch to request the resumption of outgoing UPI payments'. Phone Banking (toll free): 1800 4030 / 1800 8911. For a fraudulent UPI transaction, report immediately to Axis Bank 'through the available customer service channels' and also lodge a complaint 'on the National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal or through the National Cyber Crime Helpline at 1930'. No netbanking UPI-manage path, in-app UPI lock menu path or app-store link is published on Axis pages; *99# is not mentioned.",
